From ded79fca46132f75b1009a53ad30f93fa12ba4ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fanhua Li <lifanhua5@huawei.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:55:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH OLK-6.6 v3 14/18] arm64: mm: Introduce procfs interface to
 update PBHA0 bit

hulk inclusion
category: feature
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/9826

--------------------------------

Introduce /proc/<pid>/pbha_bit0 to update PBHA bit0.

Value 0/1 can be accepted by this procfs:
- 0: iter all vmas of this task, clear VM_PBHA_BIT0 for all vmas.
  New vma will stop bring VM_PBHA_BIT0 if exists. clear PTE 59 bit for
  all pte entries.
- 1: iter all vmas of this task, set VM_PBHA_BIT0 for all vmas.
  New vma will bring VM_PBHA_BIT0 by default. set PTE 59 bit for
  all pte entries.

Signed-off-by: Ma Wupeng <mawupeng1@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Fanhua Li <lifanhua5@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiacheng Yu <yujiacheng3@huawei.com>
---
Changes in v3:
 - use pmdp_invalidate_ad() when rewriting a live THP pmd
 - use get_task_mm()/mmput() in pbha_bit0_read()
 - add a .hugetlb_entry callback so hugetlb mappings are updated too
 - drop the mm->def_flags early return and track whether anything changed
